  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "1m-hugs",
  "description": "\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\t1M-HUGs\n\t\n\nGrasp dataset with three splits.\n\n\t\n\t\t\nsplit\nlocation\nsamples\nformat\n\n\n\t\t\ntrain\ntrain/*.tar\n1,279,142\ntar shards of <name>.pkl\n\n\nval\nval/<scene>/<object>/*.pkl\n600\nraw tree + sim_assets/\n\n\ntest\ntest/<scene>/<object>/*.pkl\n300\nraw tree + sim_assets/\n\n\n\t\n\ntrain is split into 256 plain tar shards (5,000 pkls each) purely so it\ntransfers as ~256 files instead of 1.28M tiny ones. Each shard is an ordinary\ntarball \u2014 extract it with stdlib tarfile or tar xf, no special library.\u2026 See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/kevinywu/1m-hugs.",
